<title>ITALY: TENNIS-ITALIAN OPEN MEN'S RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-ITALIAN OPEN MEN'S RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>First round results in the $2.3 million Italian Open men's tennis tournament on Wednesday (prefix number denotes seed):</p>
<p>Sergi Bruguera (Spain) beat Hernan Gumy (Argentina) 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>Jim Courier (U.S) beat Albert Portas (Spain) 7-6 (7-5) 6-2</p>
<p>Magnus Larsson (Sweden) beat Thomas Johansson (Sweden) 7-6 (7-4) 6-3</p>
<p> 10-Alex Corretja (Spain) beat Arnaud Boetsch (France   6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Scott Draper (Australia) beat 3-Thomas Muster (Austria) 7-6 (7-4) 5-7 7-5</p>
<p>6-Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia) beat Christian Ruud (Norway) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>11-Albert Costa (Spain) beat Jan Siemerink (Holland) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Marc-Kevin Goellner (Germany) beat 5-Richard Krajicek (Netherlands) 7-6 (8-6) 7-6 (7-1)</p>
<p>Alberto Berastegui (Spain) beat Patrick Rafter (Australia) 3-6 6-4 7-5</p>
<p>Karim Alami (Morocco) beat Chris Woodruff (U.S.) 6-0 6-4</p>
<p>7-Marcelo Rios (Chile) beat Fabrice Santoro (France) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>4-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia) beat Paul Haarhuis (Holland) 7-6 (8-6) 3-6 6-3</p>
<p>12-Boris Becker (Germany) beat Cedric Pioline (France) 6-4 7-5</p>
<p>15-Marc Rosset (Switzerland) beat Emilio Alvarez (Spain) 7-5 6-7 (3-7) 6-3</p>
<p>8-Carlos Moya (Spain) beat Tommy Haas (Germany) 6-4 6-2</p>
</text>
